    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/0712.2444v1</id>
    <title>A priori bounds for some infinitely renormalizable quadratics: III. Molecules</title>
    <updated>2007-12-14T20:27:38Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0712.2444v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/0712.2444v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  In this paper we prove {\it a priori bounds} for infinitely renormalizable quadratic polynomials satisfying a ``molecule condition''. Roughly speaking, this condition ensures that the renormalization combinatorics stay away from the satellite types. These {\it a priori bounds} imply local connectivity of the corresponding Julia sets and the Mandelbrot set at the corresponding parameter values.</summary>
